{
  "case_id": "2017-16-1435",
  "document_hash": "36eafa620aada5c5427432a96fcb84287ff9fafc672e724f7be81d9027ac5827",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1435",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "36eafa620aada5c5427432a96fcb84287ff9fafc672e724f7be81d9027ac5827",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36eafa620aad-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument this morning in Case 16-1435, Minnesota Voters Alliance versus Mansky. Mr. Breemer."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1435",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "36eafa620aada5c5427432a96fcb84287ff9fafc672e724f7be81d9027ac5827",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36eafa620aad-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BREEMER: It's solely a facial challenge, Your Honor. The as-applied claims were not appealed and they're not before the Court. So the only question is whether this statute on its face violates the First Amendment overbreadth doctrine. And it does violate the First Amendment doctrine -- First Amendment overbreadth doctrine because it sweeps in so much political expression in association that -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1435",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "36eafa620aada5c5427432a96fcb84287ff9fafc672e724f7be81d9027ac5827",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36eafa620aad-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: How many other states have laws that go as far as Minnesota's?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Breemer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1435",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "36eafa620aada5c5427432a96fcb84287ff9fafc672e724f7be81d9027ac5827",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36eafa620aad-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BREEMER: No, Your Honor, there's no evidence of -- of disruption either in Minnesota or these other states caused by simply wearing -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Breemer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1435",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "36eafa620aada5c5427432a96fcb84287ff9fafc672e724f7be81d9027ac5827",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36eafa620aad-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BREEMER: They're selected from the parties, various parties. Names -- a list is submitted, and they're selected."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1435",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "36eafa620aada5c5427432a96fcb84287ff9fafc672e724f7be81d9027ac5827",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36eafa620aad-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: How -- but the -- I guess the issue is, how do you know if a mistake has been made? You know, if someone makes a judgment and it's challenged, how do you know a mistake's been made? I mean, there's -- the question -- the concern, of course, it's what the case could be largely about, is whether or not there are standards that can be applied in a reasonable way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Rogan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1435",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "36eafa620aada5c5427432a96fcb84287ff9fafc672e724f7be81d9027ac5827",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36eafa620aad-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ROGAN: Your Honor, I think the history of Minnesota's statute shows that we have a workable definition. For over 100 years, we've had this statute in place and we haven't -- this is the first time that it's been challenged by anybody objecting to an argument that they believed that their speech was not political."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1435",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "36eafa620aada5c5427432a96fcb84287ff9fafc672e724f7be81d9027ac5827",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36eafa620aad-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: I mean, people go to vote after work, before work, in the middle of doing chores for the day, taking kids to school. So somebody goes to the polling place and is wearing a shirt, doesn't say anything about a candidate or a ballot issue, but a particular election judge, one of these people picked by one of the two parties, says, oh, that's political, you -- so now this person has a choice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1435",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "36eafa620aada5c5427432a96fcb84287ff9fafc672e724f7be81d9027ac5827",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36eafa620aad-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Is there -- is there any evidence -- usually, in First Amendment cases, we're concerned about overbreadth because of the chilling effect that's often undocumented. And the burden is usually on the state to justify a compelling interest rather than the other way around."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1435",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "36eafa620aada5c5427432a96fcb84287ff9fafc672e724f7be81d9027ac5827",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36eafa620aad-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: So -- so, if a group said, well, okay, we're not going to be able to wear our -- our \"Me Too\" shirt, but we're going to convey the same message by wearing all white, that would be okay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rogan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1435",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "36eafa620aada5c5427432a96fcb84287ff9fafc672e724f7be81d9027ac5827",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36eafa620aad-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ROGAN: Your Honor, that -- under our statute, I -- I don't believe that would be a political insignia."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "J. David Breemer",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1435",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "36eafa620aada5c5427432a96fcb84287ff9fafc672e724f7be81d9027ac5827",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36eafa620aad-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BREEMER: The statute does affect millions of people that go to the polls in Minnesota, at polling places, absentee ballot locations throughout the state for 46 days prior to the election, and so what you just heard, I believe, is that there's going to be an effect of chilling all this legitimate speech, Me Too, Resist, Black Lives Matter, American Legion, Americans For Tax Reform, and the list goes on."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1435",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "36eafa620aada5c5427432a96fcb84287ff9fafc672e724f7be81d9027ac5827",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36eafa620aad-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But we were just told by Respondent that it has to be connected to an electoral choice in that election."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1435",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "36eafa620aada5c5427432a96fcb84287ff9fafc672e724f7be81d9027ac5827",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36eafa620aad-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Do you have any proof? You have one person who says that this process delayed him five hours."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-16-1435",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "36eafa620aada5c5427432a96fcb84287ff9fafc672e724f7be81d9027ac5827",
      "evidence_id": "ev-36eafa620aad-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
